        "original_id": "47ca028e-d7b9-577b-8db0-31d95be33628",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Aviron Bayonnais FC, France national team\n- People: Didier Deschamps\n- Places: Bayonne\n- Competitions: Championnat National 3, 1998 FIFA World Cup, UEFA Euro 2000\n- Roles: footballer, manager, captain\n- Clubs: Marseille, Juventus\n\nFacts:\n- Aviron Bayonnais FC was founded in 1935.\n- Didier Deschamps was born on 15 October 1968.\n- Didier Deschamps is a Bayonne native and a former youth player of Aviron Bayonnais FC.\n- Didier Deschamps is a retired French footballer and the current manager of the France national team.\n- Didier Deschamps captained the winning France teams at the 1998 FIFA World Cup and UEFA Euro 2000.\n- Didier Deschamps also played for Marseille and Juventus.\n- Aviron Bayonnais FC is named after Didier Deschamps.\n- Aviron Bayonnais FC currently plays in Championnat National 3, the fifth level of French football.",
